      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `v_max` is not an exact multiple of the charger\u0027s voltage step, clamping *after* rounding can return an unaligned voltage. This contradicts the comment at line 1380 which states \"round to valid value\".\n\nConsider doing the clamping before calling `charger_closest_voltage` to ensure the final result is always rounded down to a valid charger step:\n```c\n\tint v_max \u003d battery_get_info()-\u003evoltage_max;\n\n\tif (voltage \u003e v_max) {\n\t\tvoltage \u003d v_max;\n\t}\n\n\treturn charger_closest_voltage(voltage);\n```",
      "range": {
