      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T20:26:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `voltage` is clamped to `v_max` *after* calling `charger_closest_voltage()`, the resulting voltage might not be a multiple of the charger\u0027s voltage step (if `v_max` itself isn\u0027t a multiple).\n\nTo adhere to the comment \"Clamp to battery chemistry maximum voltage and round to valid value\", you should clamp to `v_max` first, and then call `charger_closest_voltage()` so that the final returned value is properly aligned to the charger\u0027s step size.\n\n```c\n\tif (voltage \u003e v_max) {\n\t\tvoltage \u003d v_max;\n\t}\n\treturn charger_closest_voltage(voltage);\n```",
